,"color":"b","headline":"42…e3! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Pushes the passed pawn to e3, close to promotion.","Attacks the knight on f2.","The next best move, 42…Nd6, would drop Black's winning chances from 71% to 56% (−0.70).","42…e3 stops Qxe4 and pushes the passed pawn to e3.","White was threatening Qxe4, winning a pawn. e3 takes care of it.","White answers 43.Nd3, leaving Black with an isolated pawn on e3."]},{"ply":89,"name":"45.Nc5","cls":"blunder","color":"w","headline":"45.Nc5 is a blunder: White's winning chances go from 46% to 8%.","points":["Black answers 45…e2, which pushes the passed pawn to e2, close to promotion.","Better was 45.Qa1 (−0.44): the queen joins the attack: it now hits 3 squares around the Black king."],"better":"45.Qa1 threatens Qxd4+, winning a knight. Engine line: 45…Nb5 46.Qa5+ Kb7 47.Nc5+ Kc8 48.Kg1 (−0.44)."},{"ply":90,"name":"45…e2","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"45…e2! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Pushes the passed pawn to e2, close to promotion.","Takes f1 and d1 away from the White queen on e1.","The next best move, 45…Nc2, would drop Black's winning chances from 92% to 82% (−4.08).","45…e2 stops Qa1.","White was threatening Qa1, winning a knight, picking it up with 46.Qxd4. e2 takes care of it.","White answers 46.Nd3, leaving Black with an isolated pawn on e2."]}],"opening":{"name":"Modern Defense: Standard Defense","eco":"B06","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 6.Bb5: 11 moves in all, 6 by White and 5 by Black.","Theory runs out after 6.Bb5: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}